We did a commission for 60 minutes, which
was beautiful.

00:56:42.625 --> 00:56:48.166
When people start to relate to other cultures,
they have better relationships because the

00:56:48.166 --> 00:56:53.208
younger generation needs to understand they're
going to be in a group of people from multiple

00:56:53.208 --> 00:56:54.208
ethnicities.

00:56:54.208 --> 00:56:58.666
They need to understand how to relate to each
other, how to get along.

00:56:58.666 --> 00:57:02.833
Exposing them at an early age is only going
to spark all of those beautiful conversations.

00:57:02.833 --> 00:57:12.375
There are a couple of students, or a few students,
at a very young age living in a country which

00:57:12.375 --> 00:57:17.291
doesn't majority represent themselves.

00:57:17.291 --> 00:57:22.458
The feeling of acceptance is very difficult
for a young person, especially in a school

00:57:22.458 --> 00:57:24.041
environment.

00:57:24.041 --> 00:57:30.708
Learning this dance has helped them really
reduce the anxiety and feel more confident

00:57:30.708 --> 00:57:31.875
about themselves.

00:57:31.875 --> 00:57:40.041
Yeah, I like expressing myself through dance
and through different hand gestures.

00:57:40.041 --> 00:57:45.875
Like this means very scared or surprised.

00:57:45.875 --> 00:57:48.541
I would do this.

00:57:48.541 --> 00:57:54.541
That's how I express my anger with my friends.

00:57:54.541 --> 00:57:55.750
I show it.

00:57:55.750 --> 00:58:00.625
My expressions are more lively and more happy.

00:58:00.625 --> 00:58:11.291
But sometimes I get a little bit mad, so I
can also show it through that.

00:58:11.291 --> 00:58:13.208
And then, yeah, without saying anything.

00:58:13.208 --> 00:58:15.000
Did you understand?

00:58:15.000 --> 00:58:19.041
Yes, they get the message.

00:58:19.041 --> 00:58:20.250
[Laughter]

00:58:20.250 --> 00:58:21.250
...alright...

00:58:21.250 --> 00:58:22.250
[Music]

00:58:22.250 --> 00:58:26.166
It's character-building.

00:58:26.166 --> 00:58:34.000
It teaches you a lot more because all of
those art forms tap into a deeper sense of

00:58:34.000 --> 00:58:39.791
yourself, and they really help you during
adverse times.

00:58:39.791 --> 00:58:47.791
When you're at the bottommost part of your
life, art will help revive you.

00:58:47.791 --> 00:58:51.208
You have something to step on and then climb
up.

00:58:51.208 --> 00:58:55.500
For me, dancing is all about connection.

00:58:55.500 --> 00:59:02.666
Connection to three different things: connection
to the earth on which we strike and move on,

00:59:02.666 --> 00:59:07.541
connection to my culture, from which I've
learned many lessons, and connection to my

00:59:07.541 --> 00:59:09.958
body and myself.

00:59:09.958 --> 00:59:15.208
I think also connection to my body is a very
important aspect of dancing.

00:59:15.208 --> 00:59:20.041
I never would have thought this before I started
dancing.

00:59:20.041 --> 00:59:26.166
Dancing has made me more in tune with myself
and made me learn more about myself.

00:59:26.166 --> 00:59:28.708
I don't see Chandralaya confined to the South
Asian diaspora.

00:59:28.708 --> 00:59:35.625
It has to expand beyond that because we are
in a very cultural environment, and collaboration

00:59:35.625 --> 00:59:38.958
is the key for the next how many ever years.

00:59:38.958 --> 00:59:44.625
So, the more cultural communities collaborate,
creating powerful art, and I see Chandralaya

00:59:44.625 --> 00:59:49.625
playing a front and center role in there,
collaborating with art organizations to create

00:59:49.625 --> 00:59:54.958
meaningful conversations about social, economic
issues through art.

00:59:54.958 --> 00:59:56.125
That is success to me.

00:59:56.125 --> 00:59:59.708
I feel that that sense of purpose is just
heightening every time the conversations,

00:59:59.708 --> 01:00:01.750
the relationships.

01:00:01.750 --> 01:00:05.708
I would, any day, cherish all of that.

01:00:05.708 --> 01:00:11.166
You have to believe in what you're saying
and you have to execute the same, and there

01:00:11.166 --> 01:00:12.333
are no shortcuts.

01:00:12.333 --> 01:00:17.625
You're coming in to learn something that is
very deep-rooted in culture.

01:00:17.625 --> 01:00:23.125
It's not just about dance.
It's about your entire physical and mental well-being.

01:00:27.625 --> 01:00:53.750
